# Reduction Operation Implementation Checklist

When adding a new construct operation, follow the existing ops (e.g. `plane_from_line_point`) exactly. Every new op requires ALL of the following:

## 1. Mappings & Registration
- `cloudet/reduction_ops.py` entry (`REDUCTION_OPS`)
- `rd_stack` page with correct index (update all subsequent indices)

## 2. Combo Refresh
- `keep` dict entry in `_reduction_refresh_operand_combos()`
- `_reduction_fill_combo()` calls with correct `kind=`

## 3. Form Load/Save
- Prefer `build_construct_step()` / `form_values_from_step()` from `reduction_ops.py`
- `_reduction_step_from_form()` / `_reduction_load_step_into_form()` delegate to those helpers
- `_reduction_sync_apply_button()` label entry

## 4. Preview
- `_reduction_update_live_preview()` uses `preview_construct_step()` for all construct ops
- `_reduction_draw_preview()` draws planes/lines/points; point previews may include
  `preview.segment_ends` (e.g. midpoint between two planes)
- After bind/update replay, check `session.replay_warnings` and surface via
  `_reduction_status_with_replay()`
- Access data via `self._reduction.plane(id)`, `.line(id)`, `.point(id)` — NEVER `self._reduction.store` or `self._reduction._store`

## 5. Apply Method
The apply method MUST include all of these calls in order:

```python
eid = self._reduction_new_id("plane")  # prefix matches entity kind
self._reduction.<op>(eid, ...)
self.rd_id_edit.clear()
self._clear_reduction_preview()
self._refresh_reduction_tree()          # without this, entity won't appear in tree
self._reduction_refresh_operand_combos()
self._refresh_reduction_actors()
self._status(f"...")
```

## 6. Operand IDs
- `_reduction_selected_ids()` reads operand widgets from `REDUCTION_OPS` metadata
  (no per-op branch)

## 7. reduce.py
- Import new geometry function
- `_run_construct_step()` handler
- Public session method (e.g. `ReductionSession.plane_from_plane_point()`)

## Aligned axis operands (`aligned.x` / `aligned.y` / `aligned.z`)

Virtual line ids resolved from `frame_spec` (not stored in `_store`):

- **Session:** `ReductionSession.aligned_axis_lines()` / `available_aligned_axis_ids()`
  / `line("aligned.x")` via `cloudet.frame.aligned_axis_line`
- **Construct:** pass `extra_lines=session.aligned_axis_lines()` into `_run_construct_step`
- **Recipe load:** set `target.frame_spec` before running construct so aligned ops resolve
- **GUI line combos:** `_reduction_fill_combo(..., kind="line")` prepends aligned entries
  when `include_aligned_axes=True` (default). Use `include_aligned_axes=False` for
  FRAME axis combo and frame yaw ref — aligned ids must not be frame axis/origin.
- **ENTITIES tree:** virtual rows at the bottom when FRAME resolves
  (`aligned X/Y/Z axis`, type `axis`). Checkbox toggles overlay; rename/delete/size
  are disabled. Overlay uses `available_aligned_axis_ids()` + `session.visible`.
- **Refresh:** `_on_frame_combo_changed` calls `_reduction_refresh_operand_combos(include_frame=False)`
  to update line combos without resetting FRAME widgets, then refreshes the tree
  and overlays.
- **Update mode allowlist:** `operand_ids_before()` + `available_aligned_axis_ids(before=...)`
- **Reserved ids:** reject `aligned.*` as construct result ids in `apply_step` / `rename`
- **Not in export rows:** aligned axes are display/operand only; recipe may reference
  `"line": "aligned.x"` but geometry.json has no separate `lines.aligned.x` entry
